Copies a channel's newest release from an S3-compatible bucket into the store, verified against `codepush.public_keys`, so `release` can number the next build and delta from it on a runner that starts empty.

Uses the same credentials as `publish`.

Usage: leptoskit codepush pull [OPTIONS] --endpoint <URL> --bucket <BUCKET>

Options:
      --store <STORE>
          The release store directory; defaults to `releases/`
          
          [default: releases]

      --channel <CHANNEL>
          The channel to pull
          
          [default: production]

      --endpoint <URL>
          The S3 API endpoint, such as `https://<account id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com` or `https://s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com`

      --bucket <BUCKET>
          The bucket name

      --region <REGION>
          The bucket's region; `auto` suits R2
          
          [default: auto]

      --prefix <PREFIX>
          A key prefix inside the bucket, so one bucket can hold more than the registry

      --path-style
          Addresses the bucket by path (`<endpoint>/<bucket>`) instead of by subdomain, for `MinIO` and other local servers

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
